On Wednesday, October 30, 2013 11:04:04 PM UTC-4, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> We've seen that before, right?  Is there any way to easily
> make the adaptation less aggressive?  And is that what's going
> on with all the models that slow down radically around iteration
> 20 or so?

You might try a model that reparameterizes using the Bartlett decomposition

http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wishart_distribution#Bartlett_decomposition

(just invert that for the inverse Wishart). That way we might be able to distinguish between an issue that affects the inverse Wishart distribution vs. an issue that affects the way we do covariance matrices.

Ben

From u2a7f346506a3e9ff at groups.google.com  Fri Nov  1 22:09:51 2013
