> > In short, this is a Google effort that lets you use a LLVM-based compiler to create the intermediate representation of
> > binary-ish code and then Chrome the webbrowser can execute it (in a sandbox) on the major platforms without the end-user
> > having to compile anything or losing much speed. There is also an API for accessing local data files.
