Sorry for the late reply - usual conference business.

I disagree with using this fix as HMC doesn't make sense when the potential isn't smooth (recall that sqrt(square(x)) is just the absolute value which has a cusp as zero).  As has already been noted the probability of hitting the cusp is very small, but it nonzero and at a point where users often initialize.  It IS an initialization problem.

I would much prefer to see an exception thrown so that users are aware of the issue.  Hiding it by saying "we can define it to be whatever we want" (which is false) is bad statistical mojo,

