> BTW, you are going to have the same issue whenever we reimplement vectors that are uniform on a sphere by normalizing a vector of iid standard normals. If they do init = 0, then you divide by the square root of zero in the denominator.

Yeah, thankfully that should only be a problem at initialization.  It's unlikely to ever be seen during simulation.

On that tangent, I've been doing some work looking at parameterizing the sphere for sampling and it looks like there may be better options than the vector of iid normals which has zero probability density at the origin, so the problem should never arise.

Cheers,
Marcus

