Sorry, the current error message is:
"Rejecting inititialization at zero because of divergent gradient."

Here's the model (sd.stan):
parameters {
  vector<lower=-1,upper=1>[5] y;
}
transformed parameters {
  real sd_y;
  sd_y <- sd(y);
}
model {
  y ~ normal(0,1);
}

Here's the command line output:
> ../user_models/issue-379/sd sample init=0
Rejecting inititialization at zero because of divergent gradient.
>

That's our current implementation. We start there and end there. No indication that the sd() function is the one that's giving us grief.

