Speaking of initialization mistakes.... is init_adapt() supposed to start with all the unconstrained parameters at 0? (I don't recall if this ever got answered)

Here's the relevant code from src/stan/gm/command.hpp:
            case 111: {
              typedef stan::mcmc::adapt_diag_e_nuts<Model, rng_t> sampler;
              sampler_ptr = new sampler(model, base_rng, num_warmup, &std::cout, &std::cout);
              if (!init_nuts<sampler>(sampler_ptr, algo)) return 0;
              if (!init_adapt<sampler>(sampler_ptr, adapt)) return 0;
              break;
            }

Notice, the initialization, the cont_params, never gets used here. So it always starts at 0.

