We were really hoping to just get bug fixes in a quick
release, but there are a lot of little bug fixes queued up.

If we introduce significant new features, like finer-grained
adaptation, we should bump the minor version up to 2.1.0.

I'd rather prioritize bug fixes over adding functionality.

I'd be happy doing a 2.1.0 very soon after 2.0.2 with all the
new functionality that's queued up.

We could skip 2.0.2, but I'm just worried about delays in fixing
bugs, and each new pull request takes time.

- Bob

